{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfzxz6TFjeTuawpRot17W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Only manager approval is needed, and it must be obtained before the purchase is made.**\n\n1. **Which threshold applies:** October 12, 2026 is after the July 1, 2025 change, so the current $2,500 limit applies, not the old $2,000 limit (AMD-2, DEF-3).\n2. **Approval level:** $2,400 is within \"$2,500 or less,\" so only manager approval is required (EXP-1). Finance approval is required only above $2,500 (EXP-2). Under the old rules, this purchase would have needed finance approval too, but those rules don't apply here.\n3. **Travel Policy:** Doesn't apply, because this is equipment, not airfare (TRV-1).\n4. **Emergency Policy:** Doesn't apply, since this is a routine purchase. It wouldn't change anything anyway, because it only waives finance approval, which isn't required here (EMG-1).\n\n**One caveat:** The request doesn't say which vendor is being used. The vendor restrictions always apply (EXP-3). If the vendor is on the prohibited list, the purchase can't go ahead without specific written authorization from the compliance officer. Manager approval doesn't count as that authorization (VEN-1, VEN-2). If the vendor is approved or not restricted, manager approval is enough.\n\nAll amounts are total transaction amounts, including taxes and fees (EXP-4). If taxes or fees push the total above $2,500, finance approval would also be needed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2473,"cache_read_input_tokens":5575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2473},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"919869d8-96e4-4443-b495-619594b4e9c5","u